                    round1_briefing:        `CAFEPREM, a Honduran premium coffee producer (revenue $18.2M, EBITDA $2.275M), wants to take its own brand abroad with $2,275,000 of approved capital. Three candidate markets:<br><br><strong>USA (California + New York):</strong> $4.2B specialty coffee market, 6.2% growth, premium retail $18-24/kg, 120+ premium brands, difficult shelf access, low regulation, medium-high cultural proximity to Honduras.<br><strong>Mexico:</strong> $800M market, 12.4% growth, premium retail $9-12/kg, 35 premium brands, moderate shelf access with a local-distributor tradition, low-medium regulation, high cultural proximity.<br><strong>Europe (Germany):</strong> $2.1B market, 3.1% growth, premium retail $16-22/kg, 85 premium brands, difficult shelf access, strict EU certification, low cultural proximity.<br><br>Choose the two priority markets (the first is the primary market) and the market research budget; the initial proposal was $100,000.<br><br>The strategic score (0-100) is the board view of the whole plan: projected year-3 contribution and what it returns on every dollar invested. Decisions not yet taken are valued at the plan starting assumptions.`,
